Option 1: Build locally with Docker (no Cloud Build)

Best if Docker is available on your machine or Cloud Shell

Steps
docker build -t batch-processor .


Test locally:

docker run -p 8080:8080 batch-processor


If this works, you can push later.

Pros

No IAM / Cloud Build headaches

Fast feedback

Great for debugging

Cons

You still need a registry to deploy to Cloud Run

✅ Option 2: Build locally + push to Artifact Registry (RECOMMENDED)

This completely bypasses Cloud Build.

1️⃣ Create Artifact Registry repo (once)
gcloud artifacts repositories create batch-repo \
  --repository-format=docker \
  --location=us-central1

